Problem: Squares of a Sorted Array (LC 977)

Pattern: Two Pointers (Opposite Ends)

Approach:

1. Initialize:

   * left = 0 (start of the array)
   * right = nums.size() - 1 (end of the array)
   * index = nums.size() - 1 (last position of the answer array)
2. Create an answer vector of the same size as `nums`.
3. Compare `abs(nums[left])` and `abs(nums[right])`.
4. If `abs(nums[left])` is greater:

   * Store `nums[left] * nums[left]` at `ans[index]`.
   * Move `left++`.
5. Otherwise:

   * Store `nums[right] * nums[right]` at `ans[index]`.
   * Move `right--`.
6. Decrement `index--` after placing each square.
7. Repeat until `left > right`.
8. Return the answer vector.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(n)
